#, no-c-format
msgid "&doc-photo-editing; &doc-color-management;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:2378
#, no-c-format
msgid "Installation"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:2380
#, no-c-format
msgid "How to Obtain &digikam;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2382
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The website for &digikam; is at <ulink url=\"http://www.digikam.org\">http://"
"www.digikam.org</ulink>. Please check it regularly to get the latest news "
"about &digikam;. &digikam; can be obtained in binary and source format from "
"the digiKam web site."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2386
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Also you can checkout the <emphasis>digikam</emphasis> and <emphasis>kipi</"
"emphasis> source code modules from &kde; Extragear Git repository like this:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: index.docbook:2390
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<prompt>%</prompt> <userinput>git clone git://anongit.kde.org/digikam</"
"userinput>\n"
"    <prompt>%</prompt> <userinput>git clone git://anongit.kde.org/digikam-"
"doc</userinput>\n"
"    <prompt>%</prompt> <userinput>git clone git://anongit.kde.org/kipi-"
"plugins</userinput>\n"
"    <prompt>%</prompt> <userinput>git clone git://anongit.kde.org/kipi-"
"plugins-doc</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2394
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The last releases can be downloaded at this &URL; <ulink url=\"ftp://ftp.kde."
"org/pub/kde/stable/digikam/\"> ftp://ftp.kde.org/pub/kde/stable/digikam/</"
"ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:2401
#, no-c-format
msgid "Requirements"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2403
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In order to successfully use &digikam;, you need the following <ulink url="
"\"http://digikam.org/download?q=download/dependencies\"> digiKam "
"dependencies</ulink>. All library dependencies require development and "
"binary packages installed on your computer to compile &digikam;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2410
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Most likely your distribution vendor might already have packaged and "
"provided these packages."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:2416
#, no-c-format
msgid "Compilation and Installation"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2418
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In order to compile and install &digikam; on your system, type the following "
"in the base folder of the <emphasis>libkipi</emphasis> and "
"<emphasis>digikam</emphasis> module distributions. You should use a separate "
"build folder to help cleaning up sources if something goes wrong."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: index.docbook:2421
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<prompt>%</prompt> <userinput>mkdir build </userinput>\n"
"    <prompt>%</prompt> <userinput>cmake -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=debugfull -"
"DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=`kde4-config --prefix` .. </userinput>\n"
"   <prompt>%</prompt> <userinput>make</userinput>\n"
"    <prompt>%</prompt> <userinput>su</userinput>\n"
"    <prompt>%</prompt> <userinput>make install</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:2425
#, no-c-format
msgid "Important Notes"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2427
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Stage 3 is required if you are installing libkipi/libkexiv2 in a non-"
"standard location, and you must let pkg-config know about their paths."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2431
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"More specific compilation and installation options can be passed to the "
"<emphasis>cmake</emphasis>. Use <userinput>cmake --help</userinput> on the "
"command line to view these options."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2435
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Use <emphasis>-DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=debugfull</emphasis> option with "
"<emphasis>cmake</emphasis> for to provide a full information bug report."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2439
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Because &digikam; depends on <emphasis>libkipi</emphasis> and "
"<emphasis>libkexif</emphasis>, you must build these libraries before you "
"build &digikam;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2445
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Since &digikam; uses CMake you should not have trouble compiling it. If you "
"run into problems please report them to <email>digikam-users@kde.org</email>."
msgstr ""

